---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

// The home page is the project, not one event. Counts are read from the
// directory data at build time so the numbers never drift from the corpus.
const [directory] = Object.values(
  import.meta.glob('../../../directory-data.json', { eager: true, import: 'default' })
) as unknown as [{ name: string; verification: { tier: string } }[]];
const entries = directory;
const recordBacked = entries.filter((entry) => entry.verification.tier === 'record-backed');

const nowRows = [
  {
    label: 'Next gathering',
    text: 'Food hubs: the places where local food gets aggregated, processed, and distributed, and what open tools could mean for them. Date and agenda to be announced.',
    href: '/events/',
    link: 'See the series ↗',
  },
  {
    label: 'The first gathering happened',
    text: 'Building the Open-Source Future of Canadian Agrifood ran on Tuesday 24 November 2026, online on the Future Herd Discord. The recording is in processing; the recap will appear on the event page.',
    href: '/events/2026-open-source-future/',
    link: 'The event page ↗',
  },
  {
    label: 'Latest research',
    text: `Passing the farm: the succession research program closed eleven cycles and published its synthesis and a plain-English summary. The finding in one line: Canada's farm-succession enclosure is a licensing problem, not a tooling problem.`,
    href: '/cases/succession/executive-summary/',
    link: 'Read the summary ↗',
  },
  {
    label: 'The ecosystem',
    text: `The directory now lists ${entries.length.toLocaleString()} people and organizations the corpus treats as actors in open agrifood, ${recordBacked.length} of them verified against primary sources.`,
    href: '/nodes/',
    link: 'Browse the nodes ↗',
  },
];
---

<Base>
  <section class="hero shell">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">A Future Herd research and gathering project</p>
      <h1>Who controls<br />the systems that<br /><em>feed us?</em></h1>
      <p class="hero-lede">Open-Source Agrifood follows the tools, data, standards, seeds, models, and governance that decide who can see enough of the food system to understand it, use it, adapt it, and share what they improve.</p>
      <p class="hero-sub">Research published as it lands. Gatherings where the findings meet the people whose work produced them. A directory of who is already doing this work.</p>
      <div class="hero-ctas">
        <a class="button" href="https://thefutureherd.ca/discord/">Join the conversation <span>↗</span></a>
        <a href="/research/">Read the research</a>
        <a href="/nodes/">Meet the nodes</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="hero-art" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="orbit orbit-one"></div>
      <div class="orbit orbit-two"></div>
      <div class="orbit orbit-three"></div>
      <div class="sun"></div>
      <span class="art-note note-one">hardware</span>
      <span class="art-note note-two">data</span>
      <span class="art-note note-three">seeds</span>
      <span class="art-note note-four">standards</span>
      <span class="art-note note-five">governance</span>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="intro shell">
    <div class="section-label">Working in the open</div>
    <div class="intro-copy">
      <p class="intro-lede">Canadian agrifood is changing quickly. New forms of intelligence are moving through the food system, from the farm and the field to processing, distribution, retail, and the places where food is shared and eaten.</p>
      <p>Here, “open” means that people can see enough of a tool or system to understand it, use it, adapt it, and sometimes share what they improve. That can build capacity and agency. Openness is not the same as ownership, control, or benefit, and the difference between them is where the interesting questions live.</p>
      <p>The project pursues those questions in three ways: a research corpus that checks its claims against primary sources and records its gaps honestly, a series of gatherings that put the findings in the same room as the people whose lives and work give them meaning, and a directory of the ecosystem the corpus describes. All of it is done in the open. The repository is public and this site publishes from it.</p>
      <p>This work grows from two connected projects. <strong>Open-Source Agrifood</strong>, from Future Herd, follows where openness, intelligence, and control are taking shape across the food system. The <a class="inline-link" href="https://agrifood.metaviews.ca"><strong>Agrifood AI Field Guide</strong></a>, from Metaviews, follows the development and application of AI across agrifood. The two run in parallel, with considerable overlap, and neither is subordinate to the other.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="now shell">
    <div class="section-label">Right now</div>
    <div class="now-list">
      {nowRows.map((row) => (
        <article class="now-row">
          <div class="now-label">{row.label}</div>
          <div class="now-body">
            <p>{row.text}</p>
            <a href={row.href}>{row.link}</a>
          </div>
        </article>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="gatherings shell">
    <div class="section-label">Gatherings</div>
    <div class="gatherings-copy">
      <h2>Come as you are.</h2>
      <p>Our gatherings are afternoons, online, on the Future Herd Discord: sessions built around questions rather than panels, with time at the end simply to talk with one another. The first one ran on 24 November 2026. The next focuses on food hubs.</p>
      <p>You do not need to be an expert. Bring a question, an experience, a concern, a possibility, or simply a willingness to pay attention. Speak, listen, ask questions, share what you know, or stay with it.</p>
      <a class="text-link" href="/events/">The gathering series <span>↗</span></a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="nodes-note shell">
    <div class="section-label">The nodes</div>
    <div class="nodes-copy">
      <h2>The corpus keeps running into people.</h2>
      <p>Breeders who publish seeds under open licences. Technicians who maintain open tractor code. Cooperatives that govern their own data. Developers who built logistics software for courier co-ops. The directory names them: {entries.length.toLocaleString()} people and organizations the research has encountered, the {recordBacked.length} with verified records shown separately from the ones the scans only mention.</p>
      <p>If you are building open infrastructure for food, the place to introduce your work is the Discord. The directory keeps what the record shows.</p>
      <a class="text-link" href="/nodes/">Browse the directory <span>↗</span></a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="community shell">
    <div class="section-label">The hub</div>
    <div class="community-copy">
      <h2>The Future Herd Discord is where this project lives between gatherings.</h2>
      <p>Gatherings happen there, the conversation continues there, and people across the ecosystem promote their own work there. It is free to join and open to anyone who cares where food, intelligence, and collective possibility meet.</p>
      <p class="community-cta"><a class="button" href="https://thefutureherd.ca/discord/">Join the Future Herd Discord <span>↗</span></a></p>
      <p class="community-contact">Questions, corrections, and sponsorship: email <a href="mailto:hello@thefutureherd.ca">hello@thefutureherd.ca</a>. If you or your organization would like to help make a gathering possible, we would be glad to talk.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

</Base>

<style>
  .shell { max-width: 86rem; margin: 0 auto; padding-left: clamp(1.25rem, 4vw, 4rem); padding-right: clamp(1.25rem, 4vw, 4rem); }

  .hero {
    min-height: 38rem;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(18rem, 0.72fr);
    align-items: center;
    gap: 3rem;
    padding-top: clamp(4rem, 9vw, 7rem);
    padding-bottom: clamp(4rem, 9vw, 7rem);
  }

  .eyebrow, .section-label {
    color: var(--ochre);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    line-height: 1.3;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  h1, h2, p { margin-top: 0; }
  h1, h2, h3 { font-family: var(--display); font-weight: 400; }

  h1 {
    max-width: 52rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.75rem;
    font-size: clamp(3.35rem, 7.2vw, 7.2rem);
    letter-spacing: -0.065em;
    line-height: 0.93;
  }

  h1 em { color: var(--moss); font-style: normal; }
  .hero-lede { max-width: 32rem; color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: clamp(1.15rem, 1.8vw, 1.45rem); line-height: 1.4; }
  .hero-sub { max-width: 32rem; margin-top: 1.1rem; color: var(--moss-dark); font-family: var(--display); font-size: 1.25rem; line-height: 1.3; }

  .hero-ctas { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: 1.5rem; margin-top: 2.2rem; }
  .hero-ctas a { color: var(--moss); font-size: 0.95rem; font-weight: 700; text-decoration: none; }
  .hero-ctas a:hover { color: var(--ochre); }

  .button {
    display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem;
    padding: 0.85rem 1.5rem;
    background: var(--moss-dark); color: var(--paper) !important;
    font-family: var(--body); font-size: 0.95rem; font-weight: 700;
    text-decoration: none;
    border-radius: 2px;
  }
  .button span { color: var(--ochre); }
  .button:hover { background: var(--moss); }

  .hero-art { position: relative; min-height: 28rem; }
  .sun { position: absolute; width: clamp(8rem, 18vw, 15rem); aspect-ratio: 1; top: 28%; left: 31%; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--ochre); box-shadow: 1.5rem 1.5rem 0 var(--pink); }
  .orbit { position: absolute; border: 1px solid var(--moss); border-radius: 50%; transform: rotate(-28deg); }
  .orbit-one { width: 92%; height: 40%; top: 32%; left: 4%; }
  .orbit-two { width: 74%; height: 82%; top: 8%; left: 14%; transform: rotate(54deg); }
  .orbit-three { width: 38%; height: 104%; top: -2%; left: 34%; transform: rotate(22deg); border-color: var(--ochre); }
  .art-note { position: absolute; color: var(--moss-dark); font-family: var(--display); font-size: 1.2rem; font-style: italic; }
  .note-one { top: 18%; left: 13%; }
  .note-two { top: 68%; right: 5%; }
  .note-three { bottom: 3%; left: 39%; }
  .note-four { top: 7%; right: 24%; }
  .note-five { bottom: 20%; right: 18%; }

  .intro, .gatherings, .nodes-note, .community { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(9rem, 0.28fr) minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 2rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); padding-top: 3rem; padding-bottom: 7rem; }
  .intro-copy { max-width: 50rem; font-size: 1.16rem; line-height: 1.65; }
  .intro-lede { color: var(--moss-dark); font-family: var(--display); font-size: clamp(1.65rem, 3vw, 2.55rem); line-height: 1.12; letter-spacing: -0.025em; }
  .inline-link { color: var(--moss); text-decoration: underline; text-decoration-color: var(--ochre); text-underline-offset: 0.16em; }
  .inline-link:hover { color: var(--ochre); }

  .now { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); padding-top: 3rem; padding-bottom: 7rem; }
  .now-list { margin-top: 1rem; }
  .now-row { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(9rem, 0.28fr) minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 2rem; padding: 1.75rem 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .now-row:last-child { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .now-label { color: var(--moss); font-family: var(--display); font-size: 1.35rem; font-style: italic; }
  .now-body { max-width: 46rem; }
  .now-body p { margin-bottom: 0.6rem; color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 1.05rem; }
  .now-body a { color: var(--ochre); font-size: 0.9rem; font-weight: 700; text-decoration: none; }
  .now-body a:hover { color: var(--moss); }

  .gatherings-copy, .nodes-copy, .community-copy { max-width: 50rem; font-size: 1.16rem; line-height: 1.65; }
  .gatherings-copy h2, .nodes-copy h2, .community-copy h2 { margin-bottom: 1rem; color: var(--moss-dark); font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 4vw, 4rem); letter-spacing: -0.06em; line-height: 0.98; }
  .gatherings-copy p, .nodes-copy p, .community-copy p { max-width: 46rem; }
  .text-link { display: inline-block; margin-top: 1.5rem; color: var(--moss); font-weight: 700; text-decoration: none; }
  .text-link span { color: var(--ochre); }
  .text-link:hover { color: var(--ochre); }

  .community { background: var(--moss-dark); border-top: 0; padding-top: 4rem; padding-bottom: 5rem; }
  .community .section-label { color: var(--pink); }
  .community-copy h2 { color: var(--paper); }
  .community-copy p { color: rgba(244, 240, 231, 0.8); }
  .community-copy .button { background: var(--ochre); }
  .community-copy .button span { color: var(--moss-dark); }
  .community-copy .button:hover { background: var(--pink); }
  .community-cta { margin-top: 1.75rem; }
  .community-contact { font-size: 0.98rem; }
  .community-contact a { color: var(--pink); }
  .community-contact a:hover { color: var(--paper); }

  @media (max-width: 800px) {
    .hero { grid-template-columns: 1fr; min-height: auto; }
    .hero-art { min-height: 21rem; max-width: 32rem; width: 100%; margin: 0 auto; }
    .intro, .gatherings, .nodes-note, .community { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 1rem; }
    .now-row { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 0.5rem; }
  }

  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .hero { padding-top: 3.5rem; }
    h1 { font-size: clamp(3rem, 15vw, 5rem); }
    .hero-art { min-height: 17rem; }
    .intro, .now, .gatherings, .nodes-note { padding-bottom: 4rem; }
  }
</style>
